  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment is negative (sentiment < 0) or shows early negative momentum.",
    "Increase forecast sensitivity to recent price spikes — apply a lag correction to prevent overshoot after sharp upward moves.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if forecast is significantly above true outcome for 3+ consecutive days, reduce forecast by 5-10% to align with historical mean.",
    "When sentiment is positive (sentiment > 0) and price is trending upward, increase forecast slightly to capture momentum, but cap at 10% above recent high.",
    "For long-term horizons (>10 days), reduce forecast volatility by smoothing with 3-day moving average of true outcomes.",
    "If model consistently underpredicts true outcomes in early days of a new trend, apply a 3-5% upward bias to compensate for lag."
  ]
}
